Kenyan Primary School SaaS — Phase 0: Frontend View ↔ Backend Requirement Matrix
Version 0.1 · 19 October 2026 · Status: paper design only (no code). Audience: the builder and the coding LLM (Kilo Code).
0. Purpose and rules for the coding agent
This document fixes, before any code exists, every screen (view) of the system and the backend each screen needs: endpoints, tables, business rules, events and external integrations. Coding starts only after this matrix is reviewed.
Rules the coding agent must follow
1. No invention. Do not build a view, endpoint, table or rule that has no ID in this document. If something is missing, stop and propose an addition (new ID, same format) first.
2. One module per task. Read §1–§4 (always) plus only the module section being built. Do not load the whole document into context.
3. Reference IDs in every commit, file header and test name (e.g. V-T02, API-ASM-03, R-FIN-04).
4. Respect confidence tags (§1). Anything tagged [O] is an open decision: implement behind a config flag or interface, never hard-code a guess. Anything tagged [A] is a recommended default that may be overridden.
5. Definition of done for a view: all APIs it lists exist and are tested; all UI states in R-G12 are implemented; role access matches §2; audit and consent hooks in R-G05/R-G07 are wired; i18n keys exist for English and Kiswahili.
6. Tenant isolation is non-negotiable. Every tenant table has tenant_id, RLS with FORCE, and a cross-tenant leak test.
