Technical conventions [A]
• Timezone Africa/Nairobi for display; store UTC. Phone numbers stored as 254XXXXXXXXX. Currency KES, NUMERIC(12,2). Primary keys UUID. Languages: English and Kiswahili.
• API base /api/v1, JSON, cursor pagination, Idempotency-Key header required on all money and sync POSTs. Error envelope: {code, message, field_errors[], request_id}.
• Declared stack [U]: PostgreSQL with RLS, Go ingest gateway for webhooks, PWA with IndexedDB, Java/Spring Boot communication processors, Africa's Talking SMS fallback.
• Event delivery [A]: transactional outbox table written in the same transaction as the change, polled by the Spring Boot processors. Prefer this over logical-decoding change streams for simplicity; revisit only if latency demands it.
2. Actors and permission matrix
Roles: SAAS_ADMIN, SAAS_SUPPORT (S4 only); HEAD, DEPUTY (academic), BURSAR, CLERK (registrar/office), TEACHER (with optional CLASS_TEACHER flag per class), PARENT; GATE_DEVICE (machine identity).
SaaS roles have no default read access to tenant learner data; access is only through time-boxed impersonation (R-PLT-03) [A].
Legend: R read · W write · A approve/confirm · own = restricted to own classes/children · — none.
