3. Cross-cutting rules (apply to every module)
• R-G01 Tenant isolation. Every tenant-owned table has tenant_id; RLS enabled and FORCED; tenant set per transaction with SET LOCAL app.current_tenant_id; connection-pool leak test mandatory. Reference (global) tables have no tenant_id.
• R-G02 Identity. One global users identity per person; access per school via tenant_memberships(user_id, tenant_id, role). A parent may belong to several schools. This replaces UNIQUE(tenant_id, email) as the only identity key [A].
• R-G03 Grading scale [V]. Four levels EE, ME, AE, BE, each split in two giving points: EE1=8, EE2=7, ME1=6, ME2=5, AE1=4, AE2=3, BE1=2, BE2=1. KJSEA percentage bands: EE1 90–100, EE2 75–89, ME1 58–74, ME2 41–57, AE1 31–40, AE2 21–30, BE1 11–20, BE2 1–10. Whether primary report cards show sub-levels is [O] (D-07), so store the full 8-level code and derive the 4-level label.
• R-G04 Weightings are configuration [V values, A mechanism]. KPSEA: SBA from Grades 4, 5, 6 is 60% (20% each), national assessment 40%. KJSEA: KPSEA 20%, Grade 7–8 SBA 20%, Grade 9 summative 60%. One outlet reported the KPSEA split reversed; treat 60/40 SBA-first as correct but keep values in an effective-dated weighting_profiles table.
• R-G05 Audit. Every write to assessments, payments, consents, learner identity fields and settings emits an append-only audit event (who, when, device, old/new, reason). The app DB role has no UPDATE/DELETE on audit tables. Writes go through triggers so no code path can skip them.
• R-G06 Idempotency. Money and sync endpoints accept Idempotency-Key; the same key returns the original result. M-Pesa is idempotent on TransID.
• R-G07 Consent gate. No outbound message, photo display, parent-portal access or gate biometric/RFID processing happens without a valid, purpose-scoped consent record for that guardian and child. Checked at send/use time, not at design time. [A; legal basis: Data Protection Act s.33 summary, see §12]
• R-G08 Sensitive fields. Birth certificate number, SNE status, health notes, photos, biometric data and guardian ID numbers are encrypted at rest, excluded from list endpoints by default, and every read of them is logged.
• R-G09 Offline-first. S2 (and S5, S3 read-only) must work without connectivity; writes queue locally with a client UUID, and sync follows R-ASM-06.
• R-G10 Soft delete. Learners, staff, payments and assessments are never hard-deleted; use status plus audit. Erasure requests follow R-CMP-04.
• R-G11 Academic context. Every academic or fee record carries academic_year and term. 2026 basic-education calendar [V]: Term 1 5 Jan–2 Apr, Term 2 27 Apr–31 Jul, Term 3 24 Aug–23 Oct. 2027 calendar is [O]; calendars are editable per school.
• R-G12 Standard view states. Every view implements: loading, empty, error (with retry), forbidden, and (S2/S3/S5) offline with stale-data indicator. Tables support server-side search, filter, sort and cursor pagination.
• R-G13 i18n. All user-visible strings via keys; English and Kiswahili; parent messages and report-card labels template-able per language.
• R-G14 School-configured finance features [U, D-03]. A tenant flag funding_mode (PUBLIC | PRIVATE | CUSTOM) is only a preset label. The real switches live per school in school_finance_settings (R-FIN-13), so each school decides which finance features are on. The platform shows a non-blocking warning, never a block, when a school typed PUBLIC enables tuition-style charges; the Ministry has warned heads against unauthorised levies [V].
4. Scope and open decisions
In scope [A]: PP1–PP2 and Grades 1–6, with optional Grades 7–9 if the school hosts junior school (KNEC circulars address primary heads who also head JSS [V]). Out of scope for v1: senior school, boarding/dormitory, library, HR/payroll, LMS.
