API-AUTH-10
POST /auth/parent/activate
public
Claim code + phone + password; creates user and links guardian
Rules
• R-AUTH-01 Passwords hashed with argon2id [A]. SaaS realm uses a separate token issuer and audience, and MFA is mandatory for SAAS_* roles [A].
• R-AUTH-02 OTP: 6 digits, 5-minute expiry, 5 attempts [A].
• R-AUTH-03 Claim codes are single-use, hashed at rest, expire in 14 days [A]; the phone entered must equal a guardian phone on record for that learner.
• R-AUTH-04 Teacher PWA: refresh token lifetime 30 days with remote device revoke [A]. The app stays usable offline on cached data, but sync requires a valid token.
• R-AUTH-05 CLASS_TEACHER is derived from class_groups.class_teacher_id, not a global role.
M2 — School Setup (TEN)
Tables: schools (existing, extended: knec_code?, kemis_code?, school_type PUBLIC|PRIVATE|SNE, funding_mode, county, sub_county, address, logo_ref, stamp_ref, head_signature_ref, default_locale, hosts_junior, license_tier, status), school_settings (key, jsonb value, version), school_integrations (mpesa_shortcode, mpesa_env, sms_sender_id, whatsapp_phone_id, secret_refs).
View
Shows
Actions → API
Special states
V-H02
Name, codes, type, county, contacts, logo/stamp/signature, default language, funding mode
API-TEN-01, -02
funding_mode change shows a warning that it hides/shows finance features
V-H03
Payment channels (own paybill plus added channels: shortcode or account, environment, C2B registration status, default flag), add and disable channel, finance settings tab, SMS sender ID, WhatsApp status, test buttons
API-TEN-03, -04, -05
secrets are write-only; registration button disabled once registered
