Rules
• R-LRN-01 admission_no unique per tenant; format configurable per school.
• R-LRN-02 Duplicate rule: same normalised name + date of birth, or same UPI.
• R-LRN-03 [V reported] UPI is a six-character identifier. Store as given, nullable until assigned; validate format only; no external lookup (D-09).
• R-LRN-04 At least one guardian marked primary payer before the first invoice is issued.
• R-LRN-05 Statuses: ACTIVE, TRANSFERRED_OUT, COMPLETED, WITHDRAWN, SUSPENDED, with history rows.
• R-LRN-06 Promotion never edits past enrolments. Grade 6 learners become COMPLETED, or move to Grade 7 if hosts_junior. A repeat flag is allowed.
• R-LRN-07 Phones normalised to 254XXXXXXXXX on input; invalid numbers rejected with field errors.
• R-LRN-08 Imports: atomic per batch, row-level error report, max 5,000 rows [A]; opening-balance imports create invoice lines of type OPENING_BALANCE.
• R-LRN-09 Transfer-in does not import assessment history automatically (no source API); optional manual results upload is out of v1 [A].
M5 — Curriculum (CUR)
Tables (global, no tenant_id): curriculum_versions (label, source_ref, effective_from, status DRAFT|PUBLISHED), learning_areas (version, level_band, grades[], name, lessons_per_week), strands, sub_strands (name, outcomes jsonb), node_mappings (old → new). Tenant: tenant_curriculum_pins.
Seed facts [V]: Pre-primary has five areas and 25 lessons/week (language 5, mathematical 5, creative 6, environmental 5, religious 3, pastoral programme 1). Lower primary (G1–3) has seven areas and 31 lessons/week including the pastoral programme: Indigenous Language, Kiswahili/KSL, English, Mathematics, Religious Education, Environmental Activities, Creative Activities (7 lessons). Upper primary (G4–6) has eight areas and 35 lessons/week: English 5, Kiswahili/KSL 4, Mathematics 5, Religious Education 3, Science and Technology 4, Agriculture and Nutrition 4, Social Studies 3, Creative Arts 6, plus a 1-lesson pastoral/religious programme. Per-area lesson counts for lower primary beyond those stated are [O]. Strands and sub-strands must be ingested from the KICD curriculum design documents, not typed by hand; the ingestion tool is its own dev task and its output format is [O] until a sample is parsed.
