Rules
• R-CUR-01 Published versions are immutable; changes create a new draft.
• R-CUR-02 Results reference version-specific sub_strand_id. Renamed or merged nodes need a node_mappings row or publish is blocked.
• R-CUR-03 Tenants move to a new version only at a term boundary by default [A].
• R-CUR-04 "Deploy system-wide" means updating pins. It never rewrites tenant data, because curriculum tables are global (this replaces the blueprint's per-tenant schema injection) [A].
• R-CUR-05 The Ministry rationalised learning areas in 2023–24 and revised designs followed [V], so version churn is expected, not exceptional.
M6 — Assessment and Offline Sync (ASM)
Tables: assessment_events (term, grade, learning_area, type, source SCHOOL_FORMATIVE|KNEC_SBA_TOOL|INTERNAL_SUMMATIVE, tool_ref?, scoring_mode LEVEL|SCORE|BOTH, window, weighting_profile_id, status), assessment_results (event, learner, sub_strand? nullable, raw_score?, max_score?, level_code?, points?, teacher_id, remarks, client_uuid, version, state, device_id, client_ts, server_ts), assessment_result_history (append-only), evidence_files, competency_ratings (learner, term, competency/value, level), learner_remarks, weighting_profiles (effective-dated), sync_log (tenant sequence), sync_conflicts.
This replaces student_cbc_assessments and its UNIQUE(tenant, student, sub_strand) key, which kept one result forever and could not hold history across terms [A].
