Rules
• R-ASM-01 Level scale per R-G03; the server derives the 4-level label and points from level_code.
• R-ASM-02 Only the assigned teacher writes results. DEPUTY and HEAD can moderate and reopen, not edit results [A].
• R-ASM-03 States: DRAFT → SUBMITTED → MODERATED → LOCKED. Edits after MODERATED need API-ASM-12.
• R-ASM-04 One current result per (event, learner, sub_strand); every change appends to history.
• R-ASM-05 If the client sends both score and level, the server validates them against the bands and flags inconsistency rather than silently overwriting.
• R-ASM-06 Sync: each result has a client UUID and base_version. Push is idempotent. If base_version is behind and the value differs, create a conflict holding both values; never auto-overwrite. Deletes are tombstones. Pull uses a monotonic per-tenant sequence. Partial success is reported per item.
• R-ASM-07 Entries synced later than the D-08 threshold are flagged "late synced" for the moderator.
• R-ASM-08 [O] The record shape of KNEC SBA tools (score per learning area vs per sub-strand) is unknown, so sub_strand_id is nullable and KNEC events use event-level scores per learner and learning area.
• R-ASM-09 Evidence linked to a KNEC SBA event cannot be deleted [V: KNEC instructs schools to retain projects and supporting documents].
• R-ASM-10 Performance target [A]: grid for 60 learners × 15 columns opens in under 2 s on a 3G connection after first sync.
• R-ASM-11 Weighted summaries (KPSEA/KJSEA style) are computed by the reporting layer from weighting_profiles, never stored on results.
M7 — KNEC Submission Tracker (KNE)
KNEC collects SBA scores through its CBA portal; heads log in, download tools, capture outcomes per learning area, and upload [V]. No public API was found, so this module tracks completeness and produces portal-shaped sheets; it does not upload [A].
Tables: knec_tools (global reference: grade, learning_area, tool_ref, access_from, upload_deadline, format flags), knec_submission_status (learner, grade, learning_area, tool, status), knec_export_batches.
