Rules
• R-ATT-01 One register per class group, date and session (AM/PM configurable). The class register is authoritative; gate events mark presence tentatively [A].
• R-ATT-02 The teacher edits the same day; later edits need CLERK and a reason, audited.
• R-ATT-03 When a register closes, each ABSENT learner emits EV-08; a message goes out only if the guardian consented (R-G07).
• R-GATE-01 Devices authenticate with a device token from pairing. Each device caches a roster (tag hash → learner, thumbnail only with photo consent) and receives deltas.
• R-GATE-02 Event replay is idempotent on (device_id, seq); server time is authoritative, device sends its clock offset.
• R-GATE-03 Results: GRANTED, DENIED_UNKNOWN_TAG, DENIED_INACTIVE, ESCALATE. A fee-arrears denial is a policy option, OFF by default (D-04), with a legal-review warning: public schools are bound by the constitutional right to free basic education and the Ministry's warning on unauthorised levies [V].
• R-GATE-04 Parent notification on tap only with consent; duplicate taps within 5 minutes are suppressed [A].
• R-GATE-05 Tags stored as hashes. Biometric templates stay on the device (D-06). Enabling biometrics requires a DPIA record [A]; whether the Data Protection Act classes it as sensitive data should be confirmed with counsel.
• R-GATE-06 Display shows name and photo only with photo consent; otherwise initials and class.
• R-GATE-07 Targets [A]: tap-to-result under 1.5 s online; offline decisions come from the cached roster.
• R-GATE-08 Manual override needs a clerk PIN and reason and writes an audit event.
M10 — Finance and M-Pesa (FIN, WH-MPESA, CAP)
Tables: fee_categories (type TUITION|MEALS|TRANSPORT|UNIFORM|ACTIVITY|OTHER, refundable, public_mode_allowed), fee_structures (year, term, grade, category, amount, due_date), learner_fee_options (optional services such as transport), invoices (learner, term, status, due_date), invoice_lines, payments (source MPESA|CASH|BANK|CHEQUE|CREDIT, amount, reference, received_at, receipt_no, status), payment_allocations (payment, invoice_line, amount), credits, adjustments (WAIVER|BURSARY|DISCOUNT|WRITE_OFF|REVERSAL, reason, approved_by), refunds, mpesa_transactions (trans_id UNIQUE, shortcode, tenant resolved, bill_ref, msisdn_masked, amount, status RECEIVED|MATCHED|UNMATCHED|REVERSED, raw jsonb), mpesa_stk_requests (checkout_request_id, learner, amount, status), receipt_sequences, capitation_receipts (term, amount, reference, received_on), reconciliation_runs.
This replaces amount_paid stored on financial_invoices, which cannot represent partial allocations, overpayments or reversals [A]. The blueprint's reconciliation_status comment values (UNRESOLVED, AUTOFILLED, MANUAL) do not match its default (PENDING); use the status set above.
