Rules
• R-FIN-01 Payments are immutable; corrections are REVERSAL adjustments with their own allocation rows. All money uses NUMERIC arithmetic, never floats.
• R-FIN-02 Tenant resolution for C2B uses the BusinessShortCode on the payload mapped through school_integrations (replaced by school_payment_channels, see §13). D-02 is decided: each school has its own paybill and may register additional channels, so one school can map to several BusinessShortCodes, while a shortcode maps to exactly one school. [V] The C2B payload carries TransID, BillRefNumber and an MSISDN that appears masked in Safaricom's sample; other field names must be checked against the live Daraja documentation before coding (O).
• R-FIN-03 Never match a payer by phone number (masked MSISDN [V sample]). Match by BillRefNumber. Convention: the admission number, normalised for case and spaces [A]. An unofficial doc says BillRefNumber is alphanumeric and under 20 characters, so keep admission numbers within 20 characters [V, weak source].
• R-FIN-04 Webhook handler: authenticate the source (secret path token and allowlist where Safaricom provides IPs), store the raw payload first, return success fast, and do matching in a worker (J-03). Idempotent on TransID. Never block on SMS or ledger work in the request thread.
• R-FIN-05 Auto-match only on exact normalised BillRefNumber with an ACTIVE learner. Everything else goes to the UNMATCHED queue with ranked suggestions by reference similarity.
• R-FIN-06 Allocation: oldest invoice line first, category priority configurable; any surplus becomes a credit; balances never go negative silently.
• R-FIN-07 [V] Validation is optional and must be activated by Safaricom; ResponseType decides whether M-Pesa completes or cancels when your validation URL is unreachable. Default to Completed so money is never rejected by an outage [A]. If validation is on, reject unknown references and inactive learners.
• R-FIN-08 Receipt numbers come from a gapless per-tenant sequence assigned at allocation; receipt by PDF and message (consent-gated).
• R-FIN-09 STK Push: one pending request per child per 2 minutes [A]; callback matched by CheckoutRequestID; if no callback arrives, a status query job resolves it; the UI shows pending, success, failed, cancelled, timed out.
• R-FIN-10 Refunds go back via B2C [V: Daraja supports B2C] or to credit, require BURSAR request and HEAD approval, and use the guardian's phone on record, never the masked payload value.
• R-FIN-11 Waivers and bursaries are adjustment rows with reason, type and approver; never edit an invoice line amount directly.
• R-FIN-12 Issued invoices are immutable; later fee-structure changes apply to new invoices, with credit/debit notes for corrections.
• R-FIN-13 Finance features are school-configured (D-03 decided): each school switches tuition invoicing, optional services, capitation tracking and its allowed fee categories on or off in school_finance_settings; PUBLIC and PRIVATE are only presets. [V] Free Primary Education capitation was KES 1,420 per learner with a plan to raise it to KES 2,300 from FY2026/27, and the Ministry warned heads against unauthorised levies. Treat amounts as configuration, not constants. Expenditure ledgers are out of v1 (D-11).
• R-FIN-14 Daily reconciliation job J-04b compares confirmed Daraja totals with allocated plus unmatched totals and alerts on difference; an optional M-Pesa statement CSV import supports audit [A].
• R-FIN-15 Arrears are unpaid lines past due date; reminders honour consent and a frequency cap of one per learner per 7 days by default [A].
