Rules
• R-CMP-01 Purposes: SMS, WHATSAPP, PORTAL, PHOTO, RFID_GATE, BIOMETRIC_GATE. Each is separate, versioned and revocable. [V summary] The Data Protection Act bars processing a child's data without verified parental consent and puts the burden of proof on the school; ODPC adopted children's-data guidance in November 2025. Have counsel confirm the final consent wording.
• R-CMP-02 Data-subject request statuses: RECEIVED, IDENTITY_VERIFIED, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, REJECTED. Statutory due dates are [O]: make them configurable and confirm with counsel.
• R-CMP-03 Breach register stores detection time, scope, affected learners, actions and notification status. Notification timelines are [O]; confirm with counsel.
• R-CMP-04 Erasure versus retention: where academic or financial records must be retained, anonymise personal identifiers rather than hard-delete. Retention periods are [O].
• R-CMP-05 Each school is the controller and the platform a processor; onboarding includes processor-agreement acceptance and ODPC registration status fields [A; registration duties per ODPC guidance, to be confirmed].
• R-CMP-06 Audit tables are append-only and partitioned per tenant; sensitive-field reads write to access_logs (R-G08).
