11.4 How this document feeds the coding phase
After you review this matrix and resolve §4 decisions plus the §11.1 amendments, the next documents are: (1) an OpenAPI 3.1 file generated from the API tables, (2) SQL migrations from the table lists, (3) a per-view component and wireframe inventory, (4) the test plan from §10, and (5) the agent instruction file for Kilo Code (rules from §0, per-slice task lists with token-sized scopes). Nothing in those documents may contradict this one; changes go here first.
12. Sources for [V] facts
Check primary documents (KNEC, KICD, Safaricom, ODPC) before production reliance; several sources below are news coverage or third-party mirrors.
• Grading and scale: The Star, "KNEC explains new KJSEA grading system" (15 Dec 2025); Education News Hub, "How Grade 9 students were graded by KNEC in KJSEA exam results"; Citizen Digital, "2025 KJSEA: KNEC explains how learners' results were calculated".
• Weightings: The Star, "KNEC sets July 30 deadline to verify KPSEA, KJSEA assessment scores" (3 Jul 2026); Kenyans.co.ke, same topic; Mwananchi (Nation), "Grade 6 learners to sit multiple choice exams" (20% per grade, five papers); Eastleigh Voice reported the KPSEA split reversed (treated as an outlier).
• KNEC CBA portal: Education News Hub items on the 2026 Grade 4 and 5 SBA guidelines and the 2026 SBA schedule (tools 28 Sep, upload by 23 Oct); The Kenya Times, "Last chance as KNEC sets new deadline" (portal steps); Kenyans.co.ke, "KNEC to release Grade 4 and 5 assessment results on May 29" (record retention); Education News Hub, "KNEC issues timelines for Grade 3-5, JSS assessment" (PDF and digital tool formats).
• KEMIS/NEMIS: Education News Hub (go-live announcement for 9 Jan 2026; KEMIS feature article); The Standard, "The KEMIS mess" (5 Sep 2026); Citizen Digital, "Education PS grilled over replacement of NEMIS in school capitation" (27 Aug 2026); Kenyans.co.ke and Capital FM (six-character UPI, 2017); Kenyans.co.ke, "NEMIS: How to register" (four-character institution identifier).
• Curriculum: People Daily, "Ministry moves to reduce workload for CBC learners" (Dec 2023); Capital FM, "Jogoo House slashes CBC lessons"; KICD upper-primary curriculum designs (lesson allocation tables, Feb 2024 uploads).
• Calendar and funding: HapaKenya and The Standard (2026 calendar); Dawan Africa, "Government releases capitation funds as schools begin third term" (24 Aug 2026); Education News Hub, capitation increase from KES 1,420 to KES 2,300 for FY2026/27.
• Data protection: ODPC Guidance Note for the Education Sector (2024) and Guidance Note for Processing Children's Data (adopted 6 Nov 2025); DLA Piper Kenya data-protection overview; a law-firm practitioner summary of ODPC rulings against Nova Pioneer and Friends School Keveye (secondary source).
• M-Pesa Daraja: Safaricom Daraja C2B documentation (as mirrored by a third-party documentation repository); McTaba Labs, "C2B vs B2C vs B2B on Daraja"; unofficial Daraja wrapper documentation; OpenEduCat Kenya pages (STK Push, C2B, B2C refunds).
• Market pricing: Mzizi School ERP brochure; a flat-rate Kenyan school-software pricing page. The six vendors named in your brief (EBingwa, SQUL, Zeraki, Gegohub SMS, SkulManager, Cloud School System) were not independently researched; their feature descriptions in your brief are [U].
