D-02
Each school has its own M-Pesa paybill, and each school can add more to it
school_integrations M-Pesa fields are replaced by a school_payment_channels registry: one school, many channels; every shortcode belongs to one school
D-03
Finance features for public vs private schools are custom-set by each school
funding_mode becomes a preset label only; real switches live in school_finance_settings
Interpretation to confirm: "add more to it" is read as additional payment channels (more paybills, tills or bank accounts) under the same school. If you meant something else, such as extra fee categories on the one paybill, say so and this section changes.
13.1 Additions this causes
Item
Definition
school_payment_channels
school_id, channel_type PAYBILL | TILL | BANK, shortcode_or_account, label, environment, is_default, status, reference_format (ADMISSION_NO or ADMISSION_NO+SUFFIX) [A], routed fee categories (optional), secret_refs, channel_token. Shortcode unique across the platform
school_finance_settings
tuition_invoicing, optional_services, capitation_tracking, allowed_fee_categories, arrears_reminders, report_withholding (D-04, default off), gate_arrears_denial (D-04, default off), preset label
channel_id column
Added to mpesa_transactions, mpesa_stk_requests and payments
API-TEN-06
CRUD /school/payment-channels (HEAD): add, edit, disable; secrets write-only; returns C2B registration state per channel. A shortcode change creates a new channel and disables the old one; never edit in place [A]
API-TEN-07
GET, PUT /school/finance-settings (HEAD write, BURSAR read); audited; changes affect new invoices only (R-FIN-12)
API-TEN-03
Now covers SMS sender ID and WhatsApp settings only
API-TEN-04
Now takes a channel_id and registers C2B URLs for that channel; R-TEN-02 (one-time registration) and R-TEN-04 (change needs reason and audit) apply per channel
V-H03
Tabs: Payment channels, Finance settings, SMS and WhatsApp. Calls API-TEN-03 to -07
Webhook URLs
Each channel gets its own path token: /webhooks/mpesa/c2b/confirm/{channel_token} and .../validate/{channel_token}. If the payload's BusinessShortCode differs from the channel's shortcode, quarantine the event and alert; never process it [A]
STK Push
Uses the school's default channel, or the channel routed for the fee category being paid
Capability gates
V-H25 and API-CAP-* need capitation_tracking; tuition lines in V-B02/V-B03 need tuition_invoicing; reminders in V-B07 need arrears_reminders
13.2 Matching rules per channel type
• PAYBILL: payer types an account number, so R-FIN-03 applies (BillRefNumber = admission number, plus the channel's suffix rule if set).
• TILL (Buy Goods): as far as I know, a till payer does not enter an account reference, and the payer's phone number arrives masked (R-FIN-03), so automatic matching is not possible. All till payments would land in the reconciliation queue (V-B05). [O] Verify against the live Daraja documentation before offering tills for anything that needs automatic matching; prefer extra paybills for those cases.
• BANK: no webhook. Recorded through API-FIN-05 with source BANK or imported from a statement CSV (R-FIN-14).
13.3 Guardrail kept despite school control
The system warns, and does not block, when a school typed PUBLIC enables tuition-style charges or a fee category outside its allowed list, because the Ministry has warned heads against unauthorised levies [V]. Every switch change is audited and visible to the school head and to the platform audit (V-S08).
13.4 Decisions still open
D-01 frontend framework, D-04 fee-arrears gate and report withholding (both default off), D-05 WhatsApp provider, D-06 biometric storage, D-07 sub-levels on report cards, D-08 backdating threshold, D-09 KEMIS file-only stance, D-10 hosting region, D-11 capitation accounting depth.
